                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891662,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "You will hear a business student predicting how management might change in the next few years.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 15.04,
                  "from": 9.12,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891679,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "First, you have some time to look at questions 31 to 40.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 21.025,
                  "from": 16.225,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891689,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 76.055,
                  "from": 71.095,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 0"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2891699,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Well, I've been talking to managers in a number of businesses and reading surveys about the future of management. And what I'm going to present in this seminar is a few ideas about how the activity is likely to change in the next ten years. It isn't a scientific statistical analysis, just some ideas for us to discuss. One area I want to mention is business markets, and I'm sure a really significant development will be a major increase in competition, with companies from all around the world trying to sell similar products. Consumers will have much more choice.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2891700,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Well, I've been talking to managers in a number of businesses and reading surveys about the future of management.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 85.735,
                  "from": 79.335,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891720,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "And what I'm going to present in this seminar is a few ideas about how the activity is likely to change in the next ten years.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 94.92,
                  "from": 86.36,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891747,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "It isn't a scientific statistical analysis, just some ideas for us to discuss.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 100.84,
                  "from": 95.24,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891761,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "One area I want to mention is business markets, and I'm sure a really significant development will be a major increase in competition, with companies from all around the world trying to sell similar products.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 115.325,
                  "from": 102.205,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891797,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Consumers will have much more choice.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 118.78999,
                  "from": 116.39,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2891804,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "For instance, food products sold in Australia might be manufactured in The USA, China, Finland and dozens of other countries. At the same time, mergers and takeovers mean that governments are actually losing power to major global corporations. We can probably all think of companies that exert a great deal of influence, which may be good for consumers. A third point I want to make about markets is that in the rapidly expanding economies such as India, China, Brazil and Russia, demand is growing very fast. This is putting pressure on resources all over the world.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2891805,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "For instance, food products sold in Australia might be manufactured in The USA, China, Finland and dozens of other countries.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 128.06999,
                  "from": 119.10999,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891826,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "At the same time, mergers and takeovers mean that governments are actually losing power to major global corporations.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 136.975,
                  "from": 129.455,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891845,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "We can probably all think of companies that exert a great deal of influence, which may be good for consumers.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 144.95001,
                  "from": 137.615,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891866,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "A third point I want to make about markets is that in the rapidly expanding economies such as India, China, Brazil and Russia, demand is growing very fast.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 157.27,
                  "from": 145.83,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891895,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "This is putting pressure on resources all over the world.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 162.01501,
                  "from": 158.095,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2891906,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "I think businesses are becoming more open to external influences. In particular, companies are consulting customers more and more before making their business decisions. Companies are finding out what they want and providing it, instead of making products and then trying to sell them, which is the model of years ago. Another influence is that concerns about the environment will force manufacturers to extend product life cycles to reduce the amount of pollution and waste. And, in some cases, regulation will need to be strengthened.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2891907,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "I think businesses are becoming more open to external influences.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 167.45502,
                  "from": 162.975,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891918,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In particular, companies are consulting customers more and more before making their business decisions.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 174.11,
                  "from": 167.85501,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891933,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Companies are finding out what they want and providing it, instead of making products and then trying to sell them, which is the model of years ago.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 182.99,
                  "from": 174.91,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891961,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Another influence is that concerns about the environment will force manufacturers to extend product life cycles to reduce the amount of pollution and waste.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 194.04501,
                  "from": 184.285,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2891986,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "And, in some cases, regulation will need to be strengthened.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 199.52,
                  "from": 194.685,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2891997,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Many societies are much more fluid and democratic, and the structure of companies is changing to reflect that. I think we're going to see a greater emphasis within companies on teams created with a specific project in mind. And when they're completed, the teams will be disbanded and new ones formed. More and more people see work as simply one part of their lifestyle and not the most important one. And as the workforce is shrinking in some countries, businesses are having to compete for staff instead of being able to choose among a lot of applicants.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2891998,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Many societies are much more fluid and democratic, and the structure of companies is changing to reflect that.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 207.6,
                  "from": 200.64,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2892017,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "I think we're going to see a greater emphasis within companies on teams created with a specific project in mind.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 215.52501,
                  "from": 208.0,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2892038,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "And when they're completed, the teams will be disbanded and new ones formed.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 220.96501,
                  "from": 215.925,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2892052,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "More and more people see work as simply one part of their lifestyle and not the most important one.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 228.50002,
                  "from": 221.605,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2892072,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "And as the workforce is shrinking in some countries, businesses are having to compete for staff instead of being able to choose among a lot of applicants.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 238.02002,
                  "from": 228.74,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2892100,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Typical examples that will attract and retain staff are traditional ones like flexible hours and, something that has been made possible by advances in technology, remote working with people based at their home, abroad, or almost anywhere they choose. Management styles will almost certainly continue to change. Senior managers will require a lot more than the efficiency that they've always needed. Above all, they'll need great skills in leadership so that their organization can initiate and respond to change in a fast moving world where they face lots of competing requirements and potential conflicts. In most of the world the senior managers of large businesses are mainly men in their fifties and sixties.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2892101,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Typical examples that will attract and retain staff are traditional ones like flexible hours and, something that has been made possible by advances in technology, remote working with people based at their home, abroad, or almost anywhere they choose.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 256.105,
                  "from": 238.82,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2892141,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Management styles will almost certainly continue to change.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 264.96,
                  "from": 261.68,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2892150,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Senior managers will require a lot more than the efficiency that they've always needed.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 270.08,
                  "from": 265.52,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2892165,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Above all, they'll need great skills in leadership so that their organization can initiate and respond to change in a fast moving world where they face lots of competing requirements and potential conflicts.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 285.16498,
                  "from": 271.085,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2892199,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In most of the world the senior managers of large businesses are mainly men in their fifties and sixties.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 293.02002,
                  "from": 286.46002,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2892219,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "The predominant style of management will almost certainly become more consultative and collaborative, caused, above all, by more women moving into senior management positions. Many of the changes are influenced by developments in the wider economy. The traditional emphasis of business was manufacturing, and, of course, the service sector is very important. But we shouldn't overlook the growing financial contribution of IP, that is intellectual property. Some books and films generate enormous sums from the sale of related DVDs, music, games, clothes, and so on.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2892220,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The predominant style of management will almost certainly become more consultative and collaborative, caused, above all, by more women moving into senior management positions.",
                "meta": {
